                <pb facs="0659" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/5–2549</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the Division
                        of Chinese Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sprouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-05-25">May 25, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Ford informed me today that the British Embassy had received a telegram from
                    the Governor of Hong Kong reporting his conversations with Mr. Lapham and Consul
                    General Hopper in regard to the question of the establishment of ECA
                    headquarters in that city. He said that the Governor had informed them that he
                    had no objection to the temporary establishment of ECA headquarters at Hong Kong
                    for the purpose of “winding up” ECA operations, it being estimated that this
                    would require from six weeks to two months. Mr. Ford added that the Foreign
                    Office had concurred in the decision of the Governor of Hong Kong as conveyed to
                    Mr. Lapham and Consul General Hopper.</p>
            </div>
